    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the line parallel to the line $y=3x-4$ and passing through the point $(2,6)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=3x$",
      "worked": "Parallel lines have equal gradients, so the required gradient is $3$. Using $(2,6)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-6&=3(x-2)\\\\y-6&=3x-6\\\\y&=3x\\end{align*}$$",
